<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR eases to 10.83 from 10.85pct.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR eases to 10.83 from 10.85pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) for one month eased to 10.83 from 10.85 percent and the bid rate (Athibid) dropped to 10.33 from 10.35 percent.</p>
<p> ATHIBOR  DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH  12-MTH</p>
<p>	    Apr   8  10.83   10.86   10.88   10.90   10.90   10.90</p>
<p>	    Apr   7  10.85   10.88   10.89   10.90   10.91   10.91</p>
<p>	    Apr   2  10.94   10.96   10.96   10.96   10.96   10.95</p>
<p>	    Apr   1  10.95   10.96   10.98   10.97   10.98   10.98</p>
<p>	    Mar  31  10.90   10.91   10.94   10.93   10.94   10.93</p>
<p>	    Mar  28  10.72   10.76   10.77   10.79   10.82   10.82</p>
<p>	    Mar  27  10.69   10.72   10.73   10.77   10.79   10.79</p>
<p> ATHIBID  Apr   8  10.33   10.36   10.39   10.40   10.40   10.40</p>
<p>	    Apr   7  10.35   10.38   10.39   10.40   10.41   10.41</p>
<p>	    Apr   2  10.44   10.46   10.46   10.46   10.46   10.45</p>
<p>	    Apr   1  10.45   10.46   10.47   10.47   10.48   10.48</p>
<p>	    Mar  31  10.39   10.41   10.45   10.43   10.43   10.43</p>
<p>	    Mar  28  10.22   10.25   10.26   10.29   10.31   10.31</p>
<p>	    Mar  27  10.18   10.21   10.21   10.25   10.27   10.28</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 18 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day.</p>
<p>--Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
